# Nimbus configuration: the variable names the app understands.
#
# The app reads these from environment variables. It does NOT load a .env file
# automatically. To override a default, export the variable before starting:
#   export NIMBUS_DATA_DIR=/some/folder
#   python3 -m streamlit run src/app.py
# If you keep your values in a local .env file, load it with:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
# Never commit a real .env file: it is listed in .gitignore.
#
# With nothing set, Nimbus uses local defaults: briefing files in
# ./analyses-data/ and SQLite at ./analyses-data/nimbus.db.

# Folder where briefing snapshot files (.md and .json) are written.
# On EC2 this is the instance's EBS root disk (Lesson 7 design).
# NIMBUS_DATA_DIR=/home/ec2-user/smu-cce-starter/analyses-data

# Database for briefing metadata and RM notes (SQLAlchemy URL).
# Local development (default):
# NIMBUS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////absolute/path/to/nimbus.db
#
# Amazon RDS for MySQL (later stage). Use placeholders here only; supply the
# real values through CloudFormation parameters or the instance environment.
# NIMBUS_DATABASE_URL=mysql+pymysql://<username>:<password>@<rds-endpoint>:3306/<database-name>
